# mod_recovery_email: at most 5 changes in a burst

[Client] Tybalt
	jid: tybalt@localhost
	password: password

---------

Tybalt connects

Tybalt sends:
	<iq type="set" id="change1" to="localhost">
		<command xmlns="http://jabber.org/protocol/commands" node="recovery-email" action="execute">
			<x xmlns="jabber:x:data" type="submit">
				<field var="email"><value>tybalt1@example.org</value></field>
			</x>
		</command>
	</iq>

Tybalt receives:
	<iq type="result" id="change1" from="localhost">
		<command xmlns="http://jabber.org/protocol/commands" node="recovery-email" status="completed" sessionid="{scansion:any}">
			<note type="info">Recovery email saved. A verification code has been sent to it.</note>
		</command>
	</iq>

Tybalt sends:
	<iq type="set" id="change2" to="localhost">
		<command xmlns="http://jabber.org/protocol/commands" node="recovery-email" action="execute">
			<x xmlns="jabber:x:data" type="submit">
				<field var="email"><value>tybalt2@example.org</value></field>
			</x>
		</command>
	</iq>

Tybalt receives:
	<iq type="result" id="change2" from="localhost">
